{"title":"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 28","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are in geometric progression (G.P.) with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/7/27790cd3d73657777c8acdffc733d36aba72f71c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 &lt; a &lt; b &lt; c$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"107\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> is an integer, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791eb6a306b602d57b351413ffc11d480294a8d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_an$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56c5fc30887f55e60479c0442abcc7b3dd171815.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_bn$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/b/72bd2495bff748462c263a6beacebe5fa4b48914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_cn$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> form a sequence \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/7/da73a0685b94c319c641f90b53a677d45436cd5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{which is a G.P} \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/a/97a29cc36450c62dff889d5c7cc5d5a5020c9c82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{which is an arithmetic progression (A.P)} \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"328\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/a/84a4ad39310d0a43146708df9a9a83c6844e555a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{in which the reciprocals of the terms form an A.P} \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"432\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c793b844fd5276a59b5f6c5cb48e9038beb5d41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{in which the second and third terms are the }n\\text{th powers of the first and second respectively} \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"700\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a4599cf9c5dfa99b4194c4a23fab69df841f6dd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the change of base formula, the three logarithmic terms can be written as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/03847f748b58ba31c1c7c42d49d01a4f54ab2cda.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\log n}{\\log a},  \\frac{\\log n}{\\log b}, \\frac{\\log n}{\\log c}\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"41\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are members of a geometric sequence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/1/dd1b04e461c26258947b86a40a36b69638b41bb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = ar$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1f4f67748e35b44b0ceb2cc4116ee70eb1c8215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = ar^2$\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />.  That means the three logarithmic terms can be rewritten as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/2/8b27b8b0d433e6ab7769a2dbddc5fc08e99e13a1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\log n}{\\log a},  \\frac{\\log n}{\\log ar}, \\frac{\\log n}{\\log ar^2}\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/4/3841bafe659ef1f70cb2a06d138edc2bd32c987a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\log n}{\\log a},  \\frac{\\log n}{\\log a + \\log r}, \\frac{\\log n}{\\log a + 2 \\log r}\\]\" width=\"261\" height=\"41\" />\nNote that if we take the reciprocals of each term, the next term can be derived from the previous term by adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1bced85bcc47b7349dbdc2287061d345277a3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{\\log r}{\\log n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"30\" height=\"24\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffc7368e8e7b77c88b0b4bf732c88c60e27b439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME\" title=\"1973 AHSME\">1973 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1973 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1973\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">Problem 27</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">Problem 29</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Probl